  "query_preview": "..\n(Saturday night through Wednesday)\nIssued at 834 PM CST Wed Nov 25 2026\n\nClouds again will increase Saturday night into Sunday as a fast \nmoving trough and its associated front brings high chances (70-90%)\nfor rain showers and perhaps a few thunderstorms during the day on\nSunday across the Tennessee Valley. Beyond this, a broad area of high\npressure will setup across the eastern CONUS during the early to\nmiddle part of next week. The position of this feature will promote \nsouthwesterly flow across the region and subsequently a warming \ntrend heading into early December. The combination of ample sunshine \nand winds veering to the south will push highs into the 60s again by \nTuesday/Wednesday.",
